      {
        "id": 3897,
        "name": "Dragon Drive: D-Masters Shot",
        "summary": "Dragon Drive: D-Masters Shot is a third-person shooter video game released in 2003 by Treasure Co. Ltd. The game is based on the Dragon Drive series and was only released in Japan.\n\nGameplay[edit]\nDragon Drive was an aerial combat game, set primarily in large, outdoor arenas where players had to face several waves of enemies. With multi-directional dash and lock on abilities, the game has sometimes drawn comparisons to the Zone of the Enders series.\n\nThe game also has a handful of rail shooter levels, drawing frequent comparisons to Sega's Panzer Dragoon series, but these comprise only a very small portion of the game.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co6ir8.jpg",
